Inclusion Criteria:

1. 18 \~ 65 years old (inclusive), regardless of gender;
2. Patients diagnosed as immune-related ocular surface diseases;
3. The symptoms of eye involvement cannot be relieved or poorly controlled after at least three months of traditional treatment (including the use of artificial tears, glucocorticoid, immunosuppressants, etc.);
4. Systemic immune diseases (if applicable) are in a stable stage;
5. Karnofsky functional status score (KPS score) \> 60 ;
6. The functions of important organs meet the following requirements: the absolute neutrophil count is ≥ 1.0× 10\^9/L; Platelets ≥ 75× 10\^9/L; Hemoglobin ≥ 10g/dl; Bilirubin ≤1.5 times ULN； ALT and AST≤3 times ULN；Serum creatinine ≤1.5 times ULN；
7. All the subjects and their partners had no birth plan within 6 months from the screening to the last administration and agreed to take effective non-drug contraceptive measures during the trial;
8. voluntarily participate in the research, understand and sign the informed consent.

Exclusion Criteria:

1. those who are allergic to any component of the experimental drug;
2. The subject suffers from any unstable or uncontrolled cardiovascular, pulmonary, gastrointestinal, urogenital, blood coagulation, immunology, endocrine, metabolism or other medical diseases, and the researcher judges that it will interfere with the research results or endanger the safety of the subject;
3. Other eye diseases during screening:

Other eye diseases unrelated to immune-related ocular surface diseases; Acute active fungal, bacterial or viral keratitis or conjunctivitis and other acute eye infections; Glaucoma or cataract, or other eye diseases, which the researcher evaluates may affect the efficacy and safety evaluation.
4. Have used any anti-VEGF drugs on the ocular surface within 30 days before joining the group;
